    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If a bean is a dependency of another bean, that usually means that one bean is set as a property of another. Typically you accomplish this with the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<ref/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " element>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/beans/dependencies/factory-properties-detailed.html#beans-ref-element"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " in XML-based metadata or through "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "autowiring"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/beans/dependencies/factory-autowire.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "However, sometimes dependencies between beans are less direct. An example is when a static initializer in a class needs to be triggered, such as for database driver registration. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@DependsOn"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation can explicitly force one or more beans to be initialized before the bean using this element is initialized. The following example uses the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute to express a dependency on a single bean:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "<bean id=\"beanOne\" class=\"ExampleBean\" depends-on=\"manager\"/>\n<bean id=\"manager\" class=\"ManagerBean\" />"
          }
        ],
        "language": "xml",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To express a dependency on multiple beans, supply a list of bean names as the value of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute (commas, whitespace, and semicolons are valid delimiters):"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "<bean id=\"beanOne\" class=\"ExampleBean\" depends-on=\"manager,accountDao\">\n\t<property name=\"manager\" ref=\"manager\" />\n</bean>\n\n<bean id=\"manager\" class=\"ManagerBean\" />\n<bean id=\"accountDao\" class=\"x.y.jdbc.JdbcAccountDao\" />"
          }
        ],
        "language": "xml",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute can specify both an initialization-time dependency and, in the case of "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "singleton"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/beans/factory-scopes.html#beans-factory-scopes-singleton"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " beans only, a corresponding destruction-time dependency. Dependent beans that define a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " relationship with a given bean are destroyed first, prior to the given bean itself being destroyed. Thus, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "depends-on"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " can also control shutdown order."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Using "
      },
      {
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "depends-on"
          }
        ],
        "kind": "monospace",
        "roles": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
